The `TLRUCache` was failing to remove an existing key when it was updated with an expired value. I modified the `__setitem__` method to explicitly delete the key if it exists in the cache when an expired value is provided.

```python
        with self.timer as time:
            expires = self.__ttu(key, value, time)
            if not (time < expires):
                if key in self:
                    del self[key]
                return  # skip expired items
            self.expire(time)
            cache_setitem(self, key, value)
```

Verified with a reproduction script and ran all existing tests to ensure no regressions.

